{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council","id":1520616,"title":"James Sambrano's Ghost Council","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-14T15:08:28-07:00","id":1520616,"title":"James Sambrano's Ghost Council","content":"I am so thrilled that this got shared on Patreon, but we have a writeup on the Ghost Council. I hope we get to see Winter's Teeth as well!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Mod Edit: Link removed</span>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":4,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","user":"IanWatson","date":". 08-14-2023, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T15:26:39-07:00","id":1520620,"title":"","content":"This stuff is really interesting. It feels like it's a different kind of Werewolf, we learn for the first time something about Gaia's Howl and the Council are clearly an aspirational group even if they meddle with things they may be should not. I'm also curious about the Harmony and Ghreem - were they negative behaviors the Garou would fall into if they didn't keep up what led them to Harmony?<br /> <br /> The writing is evocative and intriguing, and I would have loved to have seen something like this in W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T15:30:07-07:00","id":1520621,"title":"","content":"Better. I'm still not sold on the name but a solid write up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T16:01:26-07:00","id":1520623,"title":"","content":"<img width=\"1267\" height=\"784\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ica7wuc.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ica7wuc.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/ica7wuc.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> And some more tidbits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T16:19:01-07:00","id":1520626,"title":"","content":"<img width=\"1396\" height=\"667\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/giCFUcc.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/giCFUcc.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/giCFUcc.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> A bit more about Ghrrna and how that as a concept informed the Bone Gnawers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T16:27:45-07:00","id":1520628,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\">Patreon link removed, but discussion is still allowed.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T16:31:33-07:00","id":1520629,"title":"","content":"Oh. Is the site the problem or the content? I could post just the text version if that's ok?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T18:48:04-07:00","id":1520635,"title":"","content":"When the World of Darkness games first came out, it was an American company catering to an American audience. So it is not a surprise that when needing to come up with various game terms, the authors went with archaic words in English or obscure foreign words that had connotations that they wanted. That worked well enough. There is a certain elegance about doing it that way instead of making up your own random gibberish for that term or this one. Sometimes fake fantasy words lack the sense of authenticity one wants, while obscure foreign words nevertheless sound real. After all, very few people can create their own fake languages like Tolkien and the people who created Klingon.<br /> <br /> But once the games became popular worldwide, people immediately indentified these words. So instead of sounding like real words of a (fictional) Garou Tongue, now its just a hodge podge of all these words from different foreign languages. At this point, I don't think it'd be a good idea to change existing terms to something else. They are best left of an artifact of the game now. But if you are going to come up with new words in the Garou Tongue, it's best to come up with new words itself. At least some fantasy authors are able to pepper their books with artificial words that seem real (though there are many authors who are just awful at it).<br /> <br /> As for me, I figure not to get too worked up on the specific terms of the Garou Tongue. It's probably a fairly guttural speech that can be accommodated by wolf throats (in Crinos and Glabro, perhaps Hispo). So a lot of the existing Garou Tongue words are actually much different than what is in the books. They are just an artifact of players needing something they can say that represents an important term that is unique in the setting. Less an actual IC word, and just a term of art for the RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 08-16-2023, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T23:50:42-07:00","id":1520646,"title":"","content":"Yeah, reading this and Asmodai's discord logs, it is very clear the 3rd version of W5 was made as straightforward and incomplex as possible. That and the constant CONSTANT push for SoH is really tiring to read. It feels like KM had one single goal for W5 and that was to make the Get of Fenris unplayable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-14T23:58:48-07:00","id":1520647,"title":"","content":"&quot;Muammar didn't like the spelling and it was changed to Ghreena.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oh god, he did that in this version as well! Now I know why I couldn't figure out what Hauglosk means... It's clearly a Norwegian compound word of some kind but I always assumed there's some sort of morphological trickery going on in Norwegian that I'm unaware of and that this makes it hard to figure out what the meaning is. But no, what's actually going on is that they simply changed the spelling of a Norwegian word to the point of it being indecipherable... sigh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T00:24:36-07:00","id":1520649,"title":"","content":"That Ghost Council writeup really reminds me of why they've always been one of my favorite tribes. I love their mad scientist-like approach to the Umbra and how they just throw themselves into the darkest things the spirit world has to offer because <i>someone</i> has to do it, and I would have loved to see a fully-realized version of them written by someone who clearly understands the game well.<br /> <br /> Not to sound paranoid, but I almost wonder of the name was changed to Hauglosk because it's specifically a Nordic word and thus tie it more directly to the Cult of Fenris. After all, the only place it really matters in the flavor text is when the Cult of Fenris are doing things that should trigger it, while everyone else is free to be as extremist as they want. With how obsessed Muammar is with making the Fenrir nazis come hell or high water, I wouldn't be surprised if it was some passive-aggressive way to keep sneaking it in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 08-15-2023, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T02:25:20-07:00","id":1520652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520649#post1520649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Ghost Council writeup really reminds me of why they've always been one of my favorite tribes. I love their mad scientist-like approach to the Umbra and how they just throw themselves into the darkest things the spirit world has to offer because <i>someone</i> has to do it, and I would have loved to see a fully-realized version of them written by someone who clearly understands the game well.<br /> <br /> Not to sound paranoid, but I almost wonder of the name was changed to Hauglosk because it's specifically a Nordic word and thus tie it more directly to the Cult of Fenris. After all, the only place it really matters in the flavor text is when the Cult of Fenris are doing things that should trigger it, while everyone else is free to be as extremist as they want. With how obsessed Muammar is with making the Fenrir nazis come hell or high water, I wouldn't be surprised if it was some passive-aggressive way to keep sneaking it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, had the same thought about Hauglosk. It certainly feels like a reference to the Norse-status of the Fenrir. And there's still plenty of talk about fascism and authoritarianism in the book to nudge the reader into thinking about the Get as Nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T04:37:52-07:00","id":1520658,"title":"","content":"That the Hauglosk and Malady are TRIBE SPECIFIC does a lot to give each tribe a sense of culture. One of my favourite sections in the tribebooks is the Litany section, where you can see how a tribe interprets the Litany to match their values. The removal of that sort of cultural view flattens the tribes and removes one of the best aspects of WtA; There is no one way to garou.<br /> <br /> Also, I enjoy how Ghost Council's habit of mixing cultures is present here. Using different faiths and methods harkens to the core the tribe always had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T18:07:21-07:00","id":1520731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520646#post1520646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, reading this and Asmodai's discord logs, it is very clear the 3rd version of W5 was made as straightforward and incomplex as possible. That and the constant CONSTANT push for SoH is really tiring to read. It feels like KM had one single goal for W5 and that was to make the Get of Fenris unplayable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to know what he's up to with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T23:40:52-07:00","id":1520748,"title":"","content":"I've read somewhere that Muammar rensponded to criticism of his ideas and resolutions with accusations of racism, that is truly low blow cause if he's doing it all the time he can win every dispute with team members forcing them to silence with simple few words - My idea is good but you are racist so you're atacking me beacuse of who i am. With this kind of work enviroment every moron who know about WoD only that it is about supernatular creatures will make more mess then anyone else.<br /> I wonder what's the reaction of board, why they allowed for such behavior? If they knew and didn't intervene it might be that they are scared of being called racist as well by worker? If I was truly concerned about final poroduct I would listen to both of them and make desicion good for the game, but it works otherwise I guess.<br /> '","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:02:30-07:00","id":1520805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520658#post1520658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Hauglosk and Malady are TRIBE SPECIFIC does a lot to give each tribe a sense of culture. One of my favourite sections in the tribebooks is the Litany section, where you can see how a tribe interprets the Litany to match their values. The removal of that sort of cultural view flattens the tribes and removes one of the best aspects of WtA; There is no one way to garou.<br /> <br /> Also, I enjoy how Ghost Council's habit of mixing cultures is present here. Using different faiths and methods harkens to the core the tribe always had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and I've been thinking about this. That's another strange thing about the Harano/Hauglosk-mechanic. The way it's portrayed it serves as an on/off-switch. All that matters is the state of having Harano/Hauglosk 5 or not having that. There's no difference between a character having Hauglosk 4 or Hauglosk 1. There are no modifiers here that express some sort of descent or devolution like what you get with Humanity. When your Humanity gets low, there are modifiers that illustrate the low level of Humanity. And I think it has to do with Justin Achilli. Because when he talked about H5, he said that he disliked Humanity in V5 because he dislikes mechanics that impact your roleplay. That's why he, for example, was fine with H5 having no morality-mechanic.<br /> <br /> But I think what Sambrano's version here shows how this adds flavor to a Tribe once you take these mechanics and make them Tribe-specific. It also gives you some roleplaying-hints for portraying the difference between Harano 1 and Harano 4. And I'm still baffled that the Tribe-sections rarely mention and never really get into the topic of &quot;This is how the Age Of Apocalypse impacted this Tribe.&quot;. And considering how much waffling there is in these sections in the actual W5 book, it isn't like there wasn't space available to do that (even if it isn't as lengthy as what James Sambrano presented here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:47:37-07:00","id":1520811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520805#post1520805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah and I've been thinking about this. That's another strange thing about the Harano/Hauglosk-mechanic. The way it's portrayed it serves as an on/off-switch. All that matters is the state of having Harano/Hauglosk 5 or not having that. There's no difference between a character having Hauglosk 4 or Hauglosk 1. There are no modifiers here that express some sort of descent or devolution like what you get with Humanity. When your Humanity gets low, there are modifiers that illustrate the low level of Humanity. And I think it has to do with Justin Achilli. Because when he talked about H5, he said that he disliked Humanity in V5 because he dislikes mechanics that impact your roleplay. That's why he, for example, was fine with H5 having no morality-mechanic.<br /> <br /> But I think what Sambrano's version here shows how this adds flavor to a Tribe once you take these mechanics and make them Tribe-specific. It also gives you some roleplaying-hints for portraying the difference between Harano 1 and Harano 4. And I'm still baffled that the Tribe-sections rarely mention and never really get into the topic of &quot;This is how the Age Of Apocalypse impacted this Tribe.&quot;. And considering how much waffling there is in these sections in the actual W5 book, it isn't like there wasn't space available to do that (even if it isn't as lengthy as what James Sambrano presented here).</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it interesting how much page space could have saved for lore if the archetypes were just one-liners like in JS' Ghost Council.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T06:55:11-07:00","id":1520813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520811#post1520811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it interesting how much page space could have saved for lore if the archetypes were just one-liners like in JS' Ghost Council.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and even beyond that I'm wondering just how stringent the standards for the page-count were here. Because in H5 each Creed-section got three pages. Somehow in W5 in a book with way more lore, each Tribe only gets two pages.<br /> <br /> But the writing itself is the bigger issue here for sure. You could've gotten so much more out of this 334-page-book if the editing was sharper and the vision of what W5 wants to be was more clear-eyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T07:00:35-07:00","id":1520815,"title":"","content":"Plus the archetypes expansion includes such lovely people as the Hunter of Manor Grounds, the Red Talon Who Eats Humans, The Red Talon Who Spreads Disease, etc. When a one-liner could have left things ambiguous for players to fill in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T12:07:31-07:00","id":1520828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520813#post1520813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah and even beyond that I'm wondering just how stringent the standards for the page-count were here. Because in H5 each Creed-section got three pages. Somehow in W5 in a book with way more lore, each Tribe only gets two pages.<br /> <br /> But the writing itself is the bigger issue here for sure. You could've gotten so much more out of this 334-page-book if the editing was sharper and the vision of what W5 wants to be was more clear-eyed.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520813#post1520813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the writing itself is the bigger issue here for sure. You could've gotten so much more out of this 334-page-book if the editing was sharper and the vision of what W5 wants to be was more clear-eyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>But mysteriousness for the sake of mysteriousness is apparently not annoying (or is it?). Although honestly there are much better ways to do mysteriousness than endless waffling.<br /> <br /> Honestly I thought the mysteriousness was going to be 'big battle as the opening act of the Apocalypse wiped out a lot of the Garou, and took a lot of their lore with them', which would probably have led to hunting down ancestor spirits to reclaim that lore being a big part of the game, and thus encourage people to connect with their and/or their character's culture. Instead apparently the Garou just never bothered to pass on basic facts of their purpose (or did they?).<br /> <br /> <br /> At least JS seems to have had a clear idea of what he wanted W5 to be, beyond either 'Nazi Get' or 'out for GenCon'.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T16:49:50-07:00","id":1520845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520828#post1520828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But mysteriousness for the sake of mysteriousness is apparently not annoying (or is it?). Although honestly there are much better ways to do mysteriousness than endless waffling.<br /> <br /> Honestly I thought the mysteriousness was going to be 'big battle as the opening act of the Apocalypse wiped out a lot of the Garou, and took a lot of their lore with them', which would probably have led to hunting down ancestor spirits to reclaim that lore being a big part of the game, and thus encourage people to connect with their and/or their character's culture. Instead apparently the Garou just never bothered to pass on basic facts of their purpose (or did they?).<br /> <br /> <br /> At least JS seems to have had a clear idea of what he wanted W5 to be, beyond either 'Nazi Get' or 'out for GenCon'.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's face it, a search for the culture of the past would be pretty strange considering that some tribes have changed to have no cultural traits and even with this talk that younger Garou see the Garou nation as a mistake or whatever and frankly with the apocalypse going on I think only the Ghost Council would have any interest in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T02:33:37-07:00","id":1520865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520845#post1520845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's face it, a search for the culture of the past would be pretty strange considering that some tribes have changed to have no cultural traits and even with this talk that younger Garou see the Garou nation as a mistake or whatever and frankly with the apocalypse going on I think only the Ghost Council would have any interest in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>How far can you track the history of your culture and how does it shape how it looks like today?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T09:04:00-07:00","id":1520887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520865#post1520865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How far can you track the history of your culture and how does it shape how it looks like today?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm Catholic so I'd say since Rome I think, that's just religion, but that's the closest thing to a cultural trait that I have, we have customary parties, dances and typical food but I've never seen anyone really care about the origin to speak of the truth, especially nowadays when everything offends some traditions had to be left aside, the people sing, dance and eat because they like it, I for my part never fit in with that, but even I understand what it's like to want to belong to something, however in the midst of the apocalypse I think that ends up getting a little sidelined.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T09:09:27-07:00","id":1520890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520887#post1520887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm Catholic so I'd say since Rome I think, that's just religion, but that's the closest thing to a cultural trait that I have, we have customary parties, dances and typical food but I've never seen anyone really care about the origin to speak of the truth, especially nowadays when everything offends some traditions had to be left aside, the people sing, dance and eat because they like it, I for my part never fit in with that, but even I understand what it's like to want to belong to something, however in the midst of the apocalypse I think that ends up getting a little sidelined.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The only proper Apocalypse demonstrated in w5 is how Garou, a people with a common culture and history that spent untold time fighting together against horrors from beyond have magically lost it from today to tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Outside that,the world presented in the book is no worse than ours.<br /> <br /> Also I feel you missed my point. You have a ton of touchstones to your history - your religion, your ethnicity, your nationality even your family. Who would you be if you magically lost all context for where you came from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 08-18-2023, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T10:43:04-07:00","id":1520897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520616-james-sambrano-s-ghost-council?p=1520890#post1520890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only proper Apocalypse demonstrated in w5 is how Garou, a people with a common culture and history that spent untold time fighting together against horrors from beyond have magically lost it from today to tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Outside that,the world presented in the book is no worse than ours.<br /> <br /> Also I feel you missed my point. You have a ton of touchstones to your history - your religion, your ethnicity, your nationality even your family. Who would you be if you magically lost all context for where you came from?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that I would either be what is called a blank slate or someone who is extremely cynical, as I am the sum of my experiences. Honestly, from this list the only thing I can relate to are family and to some extent religion. Now if touchstones, is what in my language is called an anchor, I imagine I would lose ground and go into survivor mode, assuming I didn't go crazy or think it was a good idea to go into kamikaze mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}